scope: |
  A top-level `object A` with NO body swallows the rest of the file on F. `objBodyToks`
  (specs/v2.2-p6.5-fsub.ssc:2238) scans forward for the first `{` with no stop condition; the oracle's
  `skipToBrace` (v2/lib/ssc1-front.ssc0:2714) stops at `{`, EOF **or `;`**, and that third arm is the
  whole defect. Three symptoms, all measured: the rest of the file discarded (`main` unbound), a
  continued def body eaten (`h` unbound), and — the one that reached the corpus — object members
  attributed to the WRONG object by collectObjReg.

  REFUTES the board's law on both counts: no `package:` in any reproducer, and no `extends` either.
  `case object` is immune (different parser path), which the entry said made no difference.

  PATHS: smoke-ci.ssc is in scope to register the new gate AND to correct the single-line-extension
  comment there, which still describes four rows as KNOWN-RED after they were promoted today.
next: gate red on the baseline build, then the one-arm fix, then gate green
